  "summary": "Evaporative emission system: the charcoal canister (cannister) sits in a two-ring strap bracket on the LH front fender skirt / production shield, and a steel fuel vapor pipe runs from the canister back along the frame to the fuel tank area, held by clips. The strap is clamped with a screw and bolted to the skirt; the pipe clip at the front is screwed down. Canister 7028024 is for LS7 and LT1 engines. Related sheets: NA9 A6 (engine hoses), B2 (tank & separator).",
